## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a scalable, cross‑platform ML bridge, handle memory budgets, dynamic model loading, and a React hook API that cleanly abstracts native work.

## Key Concepts
- React Native bridging and native modules
- Cross‑platform ML inference (TFLite/Core ML)
- Dynamic model loading and versioning
- Concurrency, worker threads, and input backpressure
- Memory budgeting and lifecycle management

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal hook sketch (conceptual)
import { useEffect, useRef, useState } from 'react';
import { NativeModules } from 'react-native';
const { MLBridge } = NativeModules;

export function useMLInference(modelName, inputs) {
  const [pred, setPred] = useState(null);
  const queue = useRef([]);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!inputs) return;
    queue.current.push(inputs);
    MLBridge.enqueue(modelName, inputs)
      .then(result => setPred(result))
      .catch(() => {});
  }, [modelName, inputs]);

  return pred;
}
```

